===Etymology===
Latin {{term|Ceres|Cerēs|lang=la}}, goddess of the bounty, akin to {{term|creare|crēare|lang=la}} 'to create', {{term|crescere|crēscere|lang=la}} 'to grow', from {{proto|Indo-European|k̑er-}} 'to grow'. More at [[create]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɪəriːz/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{mythology}} The Roman [[goddess]] of [[agriculture]]; equivalent to the [[Greek]] goddess [[Demeter]].
# {{astronomy}} A celestial body [[orbit]]ing between [[Mars]] and [[Jupiter]]; previously defined as an [[asteroid]]; now officially known as a [[dwarf planet]]; officially called {{term|1 Ceres|1 '''Ceres'''}}.

